# yaml-language-server: $schema=https://rangka-os.github.io/rangka-os/schema/0.5/module.json
name: rental
version: 1.2.0
title: {id: Sewa alat, en: Equipment rental}
summary:
  id: Sewa alat dengan jadwal tanpa bentrok, alat keluar dan kembali.
  en: Equipment rental with clash-free schedules, check-out and return.
category: operations
icon: tools-line
# Rental of countable equipment (cameras, party tents, chairs, sound systems): a rental item is a catalogue item with
# a number of units, a daily rate, a deposit per unit and a late fee per day. A booking reserves units for a range of
# dates [start_date, end_date): the return day is free for the next booking. Its submit refuses a booking whose
# overlap would need more units than the item has (flow rental_booking_on_submit, read lock of contract 0025), takes
# the deposit (journal to 2-1400 Uang muka pelanggan) and drafts the rent invoice. Checkout and return are documents
# of their own with the actual dates; the return computes the late fee and damage, keeps them from the deposit and
# pays the rest back; what the deposit does not cover becomes a draft invoice. A submitted document cannot change, so
# the state of each booking lives in rental_schedule, written only by the flows of this module.
# 1.1 handover (plans/layar-kerja.md A6): units one by one (rental_unit) for an item with track_units; checkout and
# return carry a condition checklist per unit, a photo and the customer's signature as attachments (contract 0011,
# fields image and signature of contract 0030 §5) and print a BAST (rental_bast_out, rental_bast_in). The fees on the
# return checklist add to the damage kept from the deposit. Role rental_staff (staf gudang) hands over without money.
# The data matches the handover slot of contract 0030: document rental_checkout / rental_return, rows units {unit,
# condition}, scan by rental_unit.code, photos photo, signature signature by signed_by, print the BAST, submit.
requires: {rangka: '>=0.5', users: ^1.0, contacts: ^1.0, catalogue: ^1.0, invoicing: ^1.0}
optional: {accounting: ^1.0}
